  "problem": "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nTo make green paint, Victor mixed $6$ pints of blue paint and $5$ pints of yellow paint, so there are $\\boxed{}$ pints of yellow paint for each pint of blue paint.",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of the number of pints of yellow paint to the pints of blue paint is  $5:6.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nThis means that there is $\\frac{5}{6}$ pint of yellow paint for each pint of blue paint.",
